{{Quote|There are so many! Do they all have a system of planets?''"<br />"''Most of them.''"<br />"''Has anyone been to them all?''"<br />"''Not likely.''"<br />"''I want to be the first one to see them all.|[[Anakin Skywalker]] and Jedi Master [[Qui-Gon Jinn]], looking at the stars|<ref name="TPM">{{Film|I}}</ref>}}
A '''star system''', also known as a '''solar system''',<ref name="AOTC">{{Film|II}}</ref> '''planetary system''',<ref name="Disapp II">{{SW|url=series/clone-wars/the-disappeared-part-ii-episode-gallery|text="The Disappeared, Part II" Episode Gallery}}; image #1 {{C|of 20}}</ref> or simply a '''system''', was a group of celestial bodies, usually [[planet]]s, [[orbit]]ing a [[star]]. Most stars in [[the galaxy]] had their own planetary system.<ref name="TPM" /> [[Hyperspace route|Navigational routes]] known as runs connected chains of star systems, and these routes through [[hyperspace]] were vital for trade and transit between systems, with some of them crossing [[sector]] boundaries, which conceptually grouped star systems across swathes of [[Realspace|space]] into named regions.<ref name="VE">''[[Star Wars: The Visual Encyclopedia]]''</ref> A single system could contain dozens of planets, even more moons, and any number of celestial bodies, while a single sector could contain multiple star systems.<ref name="Star Wars Book>''[[The Star Wars Book]]''</ref>

During the [[Separatist Crisis|crisis]] that led to the [[Clone Wars]], several hundred systems that belonged to the [[Galactic Republic]] seceded and formed the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]] under the leadership of [[Count of Serenno|Count]] [[Dooku]] of [[Serenno]], a former [[Jedi Master]].<ref name="DB Seppies">{{Databank|separatist-alliance|Separatist Alliance}}</ref>

